-- #1114 OVER-REJECTION GUARD for the re-export hop. Newly recording a predicate that was
-- previously dropped is only a fix if the SATISFIABLE instantiation still resolves — at
-- both re-export depths, since each is served by a separate attribution pass.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE DERIVED BY HAND, not captured: `f` is `n + 1` at `Num Int`, so
-- f 5 = 6 through one hop and f 41 = 42 through two.
import lib.obl1114_reexp.{f}
import lib.obl1114_reexp2.{f as g}

main = println (f 5, g 41)
